CAT = "sgm5Advice"; SEG = "ADV"
Q = [
('Which MAS notice sets the standards for making recommendations on investment products?',
 'FAA-N16', ['FAA-N06', 'FAA-N26', 'FAA-N20'],
 'FAA-N16, the Notice on Recommendations on Investment Products, covers know your client, needs analysis, documentation and record keeping. FAA-N06 is AML/CFT, FAA-N26 competency and FAA-N20 the balanced scorecard.'),
('The three key parts of the advisory process in FAA-N16 are know your client, needs analysis, and:',
 'Documentation and records', ['Product launch approval', 'Commission disclosure to MAS', 'Annual client entertainment'],
 'FAA-N16 builds the advisory process on know your client, needs analysis, and documentation and record keeping.'),
('For a recommendation on life policies, the fact-find must also cover:',
 "His dependants' support needs", ["The client's political views", "His employer's annual profits", "The client's credit card brand"],
 'FAA-N16 lists the number of dependants and the extent and duration of support each needs as information to collect for life policy recommendations.'),
("Which item is NOT on FAA-N16's list of client information to collect?",
 "The client's religion", ["The client's risk tolerance", "The client's financial commitments", "The client's current portfolio"],
 'FAA-N16 lists financial objectives, risk tolerance, employment status, financial situation, regular income, commitments, current portfolio including life policies, and whether the sum is a substantial part of assets.'),
('An adviser may rely on information a client gave before only if the client:',
 'Confirms nothing material changed', ['Was a client for over a year', 'Has the same representative', 'Signed a blank fact-find form'],
 'FAA-N16 lets the adviser rely on earlier information only where the client confirms, at the time of the transaction, that nothing material has changed.'),
('The adviser must point out in writing that inaccurate or incomplete client information:',
 'May affect suitability', ['Voids the policy at once', 'Is a criminal offence', 'Will be reported to MAS'],
 "FAA-N16 requires the adviser to highlight that the recommendation is based on the client's information and that inaccurate or incomplete information may affect its suitability."),
('Under FAA-N16, a client is a selected client when at least two of three criteria are negative. Which is one criterion?',
 'Whether the client is under 62', ['Whether the client owns a home', 'Whether the client is married', 'Whether the client has a car'],
 "The three know-your-client checks are: under 62 years of age; proficient in spoken and written English or the language used; at least GCE 'O' or 'N' Level or equivalent."),
('A client is 68, proficient in English and has no formal qualifications. Under FAA-N16 this client is:',
 'A selected client', ['Not a selected client', 'An accredited investor', 'Barred from investing'],
 "Two of the three checks are negative (not under 62, no 'O' or 'N' Level or equivalent), so the client is treated as a selected client unless the adviser documents adequate knowledge and experience."),
('Before advising a selected client, the adviser must have the client accompanied by a trusted individual, or:',
 'A written statement declining', ["A doctor's letter of fitness", 'A deposit paid in advance', "MAS's prior approval"],
 'FAA-N16 lets a selected client either bring a trusted individual or give a written statement that he declines one and can decide on his own.'),
('A trusted individual who accompanies a selected client must be at least:',
 '21 years old', ['18 years old', '25 years old', '30 years old'],
 "The trusted individual must be 21 or older, proficient in the language used, hold at least GCE 'O' or 'N' Level or equivalent, and be able to communicate effectively with the client."),
("A Customer Knowledge Assessment (CKA) checks a client's knowledge or experience in:",
 'Unlisted Specified Investment Products', ['Fixed deposits at a bank', 'Government bonds held to maturity', 'Excluded Investment Products only'],
 'Under FAA-N16, a CKA is required before recommending an unlisted Specified Investment Product. A Customer Account Review (CAR) covers listed SIPs.'),
('Which information does a CKA take into account?',
 'Education, investing and work', ['Income, age and marital status', 'Address, nationality and gender', 'Credit score and savings'],
 "The CKA looks at the client's educational qualifications, investment experience and work experience relevant to the product."),
('A client refuses to give details of his education and experience for a CKA. The adviser must:',
 'Treat him as lacking it', ['Assume he has the knowledge', 'Skip the CKA for this sale', 'Ask a colleague to vouch for him'],
 'FAA-N16 says that where the client does not provide the information, the adviser shall deem him not to possess the knowledge or experience.'),
('A positive CKA outcome lets the client transact in unlisted SIPs for how long before a new CKA is needed?',
 'One year', ['Three months', 'Two years', 'Five years'],
 'Under FAA-N16 a CKA outcome is valid for one year from the date of the assessment.'),
("A Customer Account Review (CAR) assesses a client's knowledge or experience in:",
 'Derivatives, for listed SIPs', ['Insurance, for whole life plans', 'Property, for REIT units', 'Cash, for savings accounts'],
 'The CAR reviews knowledge and experience in derivatives before a client may transact in a Listed Specified Investment Product.'),
('A CAR stays effective beyond three years if the client has, in the preceding three years:',
 'Traded listed SIPs more than once', ['Kept the same home address', 'Bought any life policy at all', 'Had no complaints on record'],
 'FAA-N16 lets the adviser keep relying on the CAR after three years only if the client transacted in a listed SIP more than once in each preceding three-year period.'),
('Even after a positive CKA, the financial adviser must:',
 'Offer advice on the product', ['Refuse to give any advice', 'Charge an extra assessment fee', "Get MAS's approval first"],
 'FAA-N16 requires the adviser to offer advice even when the client passes the assessment, so the client chooses knowingly whether to go without it.'),
('A client chooses to buy an unlisted SIP without advice. He must be warned in writing that:',
 'He loses his section 36 claim', ['The product is guaranteed', 'MAS will refund any losses', 'His CPF will be frozen'],
 'The adviser must warn that a client who declines advice cannot rely on section 36 of the FAA to file a civil claim if he alleges loss, and confirm in writing that he wants to proceed.'),
('A client assessed as lacking knowledge insists on a non-recommended unlisted SIP. Who must approve the trade?',
 'Uninvolved senior management', ["The representative's team leader", 'The product issuer', "The client's family members"],
 'FAA-N16 requires approval from senior management (or a designated person) who is not involved in the trade and not connected to the client, after confirming the client was properly informed.'),
('When the adviser cannot identify a suitable product for the client, it must:',
 'Tell the client so', ['Recommend the closest product anyway', 'Recommend its best seller', "Close the client's file silently"],
 'FAA-N16 says that where the adviser is unable to identify a suitable product, it shall inform the client accordingly.'),
('Under FAA-N16, the basis for a recommendation must be:',
 'Explained and documented', ['Kept from the client', 'Sent to the product issuer', 'Recorded only if the client asks'],
 "The adviser must explain the basis of its recommendation and document it, including the client's needs, its reasonable basis and the product's disadvantages for the client."),
('Which item belongs in the documented basis of a recommendation?',
 'Its disadvantages for the client', ["The representative's sales target", 'The commission rank of products', "The issuer's share price"],
 "FAA-N16 asks for the client's objectives and needs, the adviser's reasonable basis, and its assessment of the product's disadvantages in the client's circumstances."),
('A client rejects the recommendation and wants a different product. The adviser may proceed but must:',
 'Document it and warn him', ['Refuse to transact for him', 'Charge him a penalty fee', 'Report him to MAS'],
 "FAA-N16 lets the adviser carry out the client's choice, but it must document the decision and highlight in writing that the client is responsible for the suitability of the product."),
('When must the adviser give the client a summary of the fact-find and the recommendation with its basis?',
 'Before he signs the application', ['Within a month of the sale', 'Only when the policy is issued', 'Only at the annual review'],
 'FAA-N16 requires the summary document before the client signs the application form or consents to dispose of a product.'),
('For a life policy recommendation, the adviser must give the client the cover page, product summary and:',
 'Policy illustration', ["Insurer's annual report", "Agent's contract", 'Reinsurance treaty'],
 'FAA-N16 lists the cover page, product summary, policy illustration, bundled product disclosure document and product highlights sheet, where available.'),
('For a unit trust recommendation, the client must receive the prospectus and the:',
 'Product highlights sheet', ["Fund's trust deed only", "Manager's staff payroll", 'SGX listing manual'],
 'For a collective investment scheme, FAA-N16 requires the prospectus or profile statement and the product highlights sheet, if applicable.'),
('When recommending a bundled life product, the adviser must disclose the option of buying:',
 'Comparable term life cover', ['A unit trust instead', 'A fixed deposit account', 'Shares in the insurer'],
 'FAA-N16 asks the adviser to disclose, as set out in the bundled product disclosure document, the option of a comparable term life insurance product.'),
('Under FAA-N16, a switch recommendation is detrimental where the client:',
 'Pays costs for no benefit', ['Gets better cover for less', 'Moves to a more suitable plan', 'Keeps both old and new plans'],
 'Factors include a penalty for ending the original product, transaction costs without real benefit, lower or equal benefit at a higher cost, and a less suitable replacement.'),
('Before a client switches from one designated investment product to another, the adviser must disclose in writing:',
 'Any fees for switching', ['Its own monthly sales target', "The product's past awards", "The issuer's dividend policy"],
 'FAA-N16 requires written disclosure of any fee or charge the client would bear for switching, so the client can decide on an informed basis.'),
('From 29 December 2025, a transaction for a selected client needs a documentation review and a call-back unless:',
 'A supervisor was present throughout', ['The client is over 70 years old', 'The premium is paid in cash', 'The policy has no riders attached'],
 'FAA-N16 requires both pre-transaction checks for selected clients and clients of selected representatives, but the call-back is not needed if a supervisor was present throughout.'),
('Who may conduct a pre-transaction call-back?',
 'Non-sales staff', ['The representative who sold it', "The client's relative", "The product's fund manager"],
 'FAA-N16 requires the checks to be done by a supervisor of the representative, non-sales staff, or an effective third party service provider.'),
('A documentation review allowed to finish after the transaction must be completed within the free-look period or, if none:',
 '5 business days', ['30 calendar days', '1 business day', '3 months'],
 'FAA-N16 lets the review run after the effective date only in set conditions, and it must then finish within the free-look or cancellation period, or 5 business days where there is none.'),
]
